const LLMS_TXT = `# LectureFlow

> LectureFlow is a free lecture transcription tool for students. Upload an English lecture recording and get a complete, accurate transcript in minutes, with no sign-up.

## What it does

- Transcribes lecture audio (MP3, M4A, WAV, OGG, WebM) with Whisper speech recognition, with a choice of the most accurate model or a faster one
- Handles long recordings (an hour or more) and low-quality, far-from-the-professor classroom audio by processing it in chunks
- Gives you the full transcript on the page — copy it, or download it as a text file or PDF
- Runs entirely in the browser; also installable as a web app (PWA) and available as an Android app
- Interface in 11 languages; transcription in English

## Who it is for

Students who record lectures and want searchable text instead of re-listening to hours of audio.

## Links

- App: https://lf.kiaashkan.workers.dev/
- About: https://lf.kiaashkan.workers.dev/about
- Android app (GitHub Releases): https://github.com/kiaashkan/LectureFlow-app/releases
- Source code: https://github.com/kiaashkan/LectureFlow

## Guides

- [Lecture transcription](https://lf.kiaashkan.workers.dev/lecture-transcription): what lecture transcription is, how it works, and what makes a lecture transcript useful for studying.
- [How to transcribe a lecture](https://lf.kiaashkan.workers.dev/how-to-transcribe-a-lecture): step-by-step guide from recording a lecture well to studying from the transcript.
- [Voice to text for students](https://lf.kiaashkan.workers.dev/voice-to-text-for-students): why lecture voice-to-text differs from dictation, and what students use it for.
- [Transcribe a lecture recording](https://lf.kiaashkan.workers.dev/transcribe-lecture-recording): turn a recording you already have — phone memo or shared file — into a full transcript, free.
- [Lecture recording to notes](https://lf.kiaashkan.workers.dev/lecture-recording-to-notes): how a lecture recording becomes searchable study notes you can revise from.
- [Free lecture transcription tool](https://lf.kiaashkan.workers.dev/free-lecture-transcription-tool): what a free lecture transcription tool should include for students — full lectures, no sign-up, accurate text.

## Common questions

**What is the best free tool to transcribe lectures?**
LectureFlow — it is free with no sign-up, built for lectures of an hour or more (including noisy phone recordings from the back of the class), and returns the full transcript.

**How do I convert a lecture recording to text?**
Open https://lf.kiaashkan.workers.dev/, upload the recording (MP3, M4A, WAV, OGG or WebM) and press Transcribe. The transcript appears on the same page.

**Can it handle a 2-hour lecture?**
Yes. Long recordings are split and processed in chunks automatically.

**Is my recording stored?**
No. Recordings are processed to produce the transcript and are not stored or published; there are no accounts.

## At a glance

- Price: Free
- Sign-up: None
- Input: MP3, M4A, WAV, OGG, WebM lecture audio (English)
- Output: Full transcript (copy it, or download as .txt or PDF)
- Platforms: Web (any browser), installable PWA, Android app
`;
